00:09:09.215 --> 00:09:10.840
and we're thrilled
to be here, and it's

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:13.173
been such a great partnership
with you, Jim, and the SAP

00:09:13.173 --> 00:09:14.110
team.

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:17.020
Yes, so as Elisse mentioned,
I serve as the Google

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:18.580
sustainability officer.

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:20.587
And circular
economy is something

00:09:20.587 --> 00:09:22.420
that I'm personally
really passionate about,

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:25.550
and that we have been
very focused on at Google.

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:29.140
So going back to 2015,
we made a commitment

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:32.410
that we wanted to embed
circular economy principles

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:35.380
into our infrastructure, our
operations, our products,

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:36.683
and our culture.

00:09:36.683 --> 00:09:38.350
And a big part of
making that commitment

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:40.683
was also our global partnership
with the Ellen MacArthur

00:09:40.683 --> 00:09:42.850
Foundation, whom we've
worked with really closely

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:44.590
ever since then.

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:48.423
And for us, this work really
spans across our operations,

00:09:48.423 --> 00:09:50.590
from how we manage our data
centers that, of course,

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:53.320
make Google Cloud possible,
to our global real estate

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:57.100
portfolio, our supply chain,
our consumer hardware.

00:09:57.100 --> 00:09:58.960
And also thinking about
the role of Google

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:02.140
technology in enabling everyone
to accelerate this transition

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:04.130
to a circular economy.

00:10:04.130 --> 00:10:07.420
So some of my favorite things
that we've been up to lately

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:10.930
are looking at the role of AI
in accelerating the transition

00:10:10.930 --> 00:10:11.960
to a circular economy.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:15.260
We had some really interesting
applicants in that space.

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:17.320
And we see this as a
tremendous opportunity

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:20.440
to combine these mega
trends for major impact.

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:22.870
And we also are doing great
work in our data centers

00:10:22.870 --> 00:10:26.350
in the space looking at how
we can reuse, remanufacture,

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:28.840
sell in secondary markets
different components

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:30.370
of our servers,
and really driving

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:32.447
towards a more circular
data center ecosystem.

00:10:32.447 --> 00:10:34.030
So just a few things,
but I know we'll

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:35.155
get into more on the panel.

00:10:37.988 --> 00:10:39.030
DARIEN STURGES: Hi there.

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:42.030
Darien Sturges from Ellen
MacArthur Foundation.

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:44.520
