MacArthur Foundation,

00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:17.190
which is an organization that
is about eight years old now

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:20.130
with the mission statement of
accelerating the transition

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:21.830
to a circular economy.

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:26.250
And we can get into a little
bit about what that means later,

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:31.140
but the broad brushstrokes
are we work with organizations

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:33.090
around the world from
the private sector,

00:11:33.090 --> 00:11:36.700
big global companies like
Google, universities.

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:38.700
We work with the public
sector, both at the city

00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:42.360
level and the national
level, to drive change.

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:47.130
And that runs the gamut from
very tangible projects--

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:51.600
Kate gave a few examples-- to
more thought leadership pieces

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:55.320
about what technology can
mean for sustainability

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:57.810
and the circular
economy, from cloud,

00:11:57.810 --> 00:12:00.810
from artificial
intelligence, et cetera.

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:05.970
So that's an overview of the
Ellen MacArthur Foundation.

00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:09.270
Again, I'd like to say it's
great to be here and see

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:12.150
so much interest in the work.

